<h1>About howto.email</h1>
<p>howto.email is a free, open-source, vendor-neutral knowledge base and troubleshooting toolbox for email infrastructure. It is built to be useful whether you are learning how email works, administering a production environment, or trying to understand why a particular configuration behaves the way it does.</p>
<p>Coverage includes SMTP, DNS, SPF, DKIM, DMARC, TLS, deliverability, mailbox protocols, security, troubleshooting, Microsoft 365, Google Workspace, application sending, incident response, and modern email operations.</p>
<h2>Documentation and tools</h2>
<p>The site is organized around a simple workflow: learn the concept, look up the technical details, inspect the environment, understand the result, make an appropriate change, and test again.</p>
<p>Interactive tools such as Domain Check complement the documentation. They inspect public information and connect findings to relevant howto.email articles. The tools are not intended to replace the documentation with a single score or a black-box recommendation.</p>
<h2>Vendor neutral by design</h2>
<p>Email crosses products, providers, networks, and standards. howto.email therefore focuses on protocols and observable behavior first. Vendor-specific documentation is included where implementation details matter, but references to a company, service, or product do not imply endorsement.</p>
<h2>Open and practical</h2>
<p>The project favors primary standards, authoritative documentation, reproducible troubleshooting steps, and explanations that show the evidence behind a finding. Tools are designed to work without requiring an account or turning the site into a hosted email-management platform.</p>
